    "preamble": "S.Joseph Selvaraj Fernando vs Government Of Tamil Nadu on 29 November, 2024 Author: Battu Devanand Bench: Battu Devanand W.P.No IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT MADRAS DATED :29.11.2024 CORAM: THE HON'BLE MR.JUSTICE BATTU DEVANAND W.P.No.26002 of 2018 and W.M.P.Nos.30214 & 30218 of 2018 S.Joseph Selvaraj Fernando ... Petitioner Vs. 1.Government of Tamil Nadu Rep.by Principal Secretary to Government, Health and Family Welfare (AB2) Department, Chennai 9. 2.The Commissioner of Food Safety, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Department, 359, Anna Salai, Chennai 600 006. 3.The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Department, Chennai District , 33, West Jones Road, Saidapet, Chennai 600 015. 4.Director of Public Health and Preventive Medicine, Public Health and Preventive Medicine Department, Chennai 600 006. 5.The Project Officer, National Filaria Control Unit, Chengalpattu 603 002. ... Respondents S.Joseph Selvaraj Fernando vs Government Of Tamil Nadu on 29 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50873348/ 1 PRAYER: Writ petition has been filed under Article 226 of the Constitu https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Page No.1 of 4 W India praying for issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus after for the records from the 1st respondent relating to the proceedings of respondent dated 03.07.2018 bearing R.No.4049/2018/S1/ FSSA/ 41-1 and consequential proceedings of the 3rd respondent dated 04.07.2018 beari reference ROC No. 5268/ DO/ CC/ 2018 and quash the same as illegal arbitrary malafide without jurisdiction and to consequently d respondents 2 and 3 to continue to the petitioner in the 2 nd department as it was done in the case of other Food Safety Officer app along with the petitioner whose name was gazette on 20.04.2012 and con in the 2nd respondent benefits, pay all monetary service and other ser benefits together with arrears, revision etc., which the petitioner wo been entitled to had the impugned proceedings were not passed by the 2 3rd respondents . For Petitioner : Mr.K.Srinivasa Murthy For Respondents : Mr.K.Tippusulthan Government Advocate 9. S.Joseph Selvaraj Fernando vs Government Of Tamil Nadu on 29 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50873348/ 2 2.The Commissioner of Food Safety, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Department, 359, Anna Salai, Chennai 600 006. 3.The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Department, Chennai District, 33, West Jones Road, Saidapet, Chennai 600 015. 4.Director of Public Health and Preventive Medicine, Public Health and Preventive Medicine Department, Chennai 600 006. 5.The Project Officer, National Filaria Control Unit, Chengalpattu 603 002. BATTU DEVANAND,J. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis sms and W.M.P.Nos.30214 & 30218 of 2018 29.11.2024 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis S.Joseph Selvaraj Fernando vs Government Of Tamil Nadu on 29 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50873348/ 3",
